  "# ADR-2607246100: Revenue agent loop capital-allocation governor\n\n**Status:** accepted\n**Date:** 2026-07-24\n**Decider:** Jun Kawasaki\n\n## Context\n\nThe portfolio has many products and substantial implementation capacity, but verified external revenue remains zero. The limiting system is distribution and closing: named buyer selection, qualified contact, discovery, proposal, contract, payment, fulfillment, retention, and referral do not yet form a repeatable path.\n\nA nominal JPY 3,000,000 budget creates a risk of confusing activity with evidence. Product development, advertising, and investor outreach can all consume the budget without producing customer gross profit. No investment can guarantee immediate profit, so capital must be governed as a sequence of falsifiable experiments rather than as one approved spend.\n\nThe existing revenue agent loop ranks actions and enforces commercial hard gates. It does not yet define capital tranches, allowable customer-acquisition cost, payback gates, or the distinction between customer revenue and financing cash.\n\n## Decision\n\n### 1. Objective and offer\n\nOptimize for verified cash gross profit from a non-owner customer, then for repeatable 90-day contribution margin. Do not build another AI web-marketing SaaS before proving demand. Use AI internally for account research, draft personalization, call summaries, follow-up, CRM scoring, and next-best-action; a human remains responsible for target approval, external send, discovery, price negotiation, and contract close.\n\nThe initial offer ladder is a hypothesis, not booked revenue:\n\n- paid diagnostic: JPY 20,000, one week, fully credited to implementation;\n- AI Revenue/Sales Pipeline implementation sprint: JPY 300,000–500,000, 30 days;\n- managed improvement: JPY 80,000 per month after implementation.\n\nThe diagnostic is not a standalone scale target. At an assumed 80% contribution margin, recovering JPY 3,000,000 through JPY 20,000 diagnostics alone would require 188 customers. A JPY 300,000 implementation plus two JPY 80,000 months yields JPY 460,000 revenue and JPY 368,000 assumed contribution, requiring about nine customers; at JPY 500,000 implementation it yields JPY 660,000 revenue and JPY 528,000 assumed contribution, requiring about six. These are planning assumptions and must be replaced by observed delivery cost, fees, refunds, taxes, retention, and founder hours.\n\n### 2. Capital tranches\n\nJPY 3,000,000 is a maximum envelope. Unreleased capital remains a reserve.\n\n| Tranche | Maximum | Release condition | Purpose |\n|---|---:|---|---|\n| T1 | JPY 300,000 | this ADR accepted | one segment, 100 named accounts, up to 200 personalized contacts, five qualified discoveries, three proposals, one verified paid implementation or diagnostic with an agreed implementation next step |\n| T2 | JPY 700,000 | first verified non-owner payment and successful fulfillment | produce a case study, close customers two and three through substantially the same buyer/problem/offer path, measure actual delivery cost |\n| T3 | JPY 1,000,000 | at least two customers and evidence that the close is repeatable | add sales/delivery capacity and run small paid-channel tests using only the manually proven message |\n| T4 | JPY 1,000,000 | observed acquisition payback no longer than three months and positive contribution after delivery cost | scale the winning channel and preserve working-capital coverage |\n\nRelease is a ceiling, not a spending target. Every external financial action still requires the existing approval and commercial gates.\n\n### 3. Initial envelope by use\n\nThe planning envelope is: JPY 900,000 founder-led sales support; JPY 600,000 fulfillment/customer success; JPY 400,000 proof assets, demo, landing page, ROI material, and case studies; JPY 300,000 paid-channel experiments; JPY 300,000 CRM and measurement automation; JPY 200,000 remaining legal, registration, and tax work; JPY 300,000 reserve. A later tranche may reallocate these maxima when external evidence changes, but a run must record the change and rationale before commitment.\n\n### 4. Unit-economics governor\n\nEvery proposed acquisition action records:\n\n```\ncontribution = collected revenue - refunds - payment fees - variable delivery cost\nCAC = attributable sales + marketing cash spend / new paying customers\npayback_months = CAC / monthly contribution after initial contribution\ncapital_efficiency = expected contribution * evidence confidence / cash at risk\n```\n\nFounder hours are recorded separately and also valued with an explicit shadow hourly rate for comparison. Missing inputs are `unknown`, never zero. Paid acquisition remains held until founder-led/manual sales produces at least one verified non-owner payment and fulfillment. T4 remains held unless observed payback is at most three months.\n\n### 5. Tick contract\n\nEach business tick executes:\n\n```\nOBSERVE cash, funnel, delivery cost, gates, and released/committed/spent capital\n→ SCORE action-level cash, profit, confidence, and capital efficiency\n→ GOVERN commercial safety and tranche eligibility\n→ SELECT one action, WIP=1\n→ PROPOSE human-reviewed external effects\n→ EXECUTE one bounded experiment\n→ VERIFY receipts, payment, fulfillment, contribution, and funnel change\n→ DECIDE scale | continue | change | stop\n→ RECORD append-only run and updated posterior\n```\n\nA run cannot report success because copy, code, a list, or a campaign was created. Success requires the external evidence fixed at run start. If 100 qualified named accounts produce fewer than five qualified discoveries, change segment/message/channel rather than increase spend. If the run reaches 14 days or 20 person-hours without its external evidence, stop or change. Never spend the next tranche to rescue an unproven prior tranche.\n\n### 6. Financing lane\n\nInvestor outreach belongs to a separately scored `financing` objective with runway, dilution, control, and probability-of-close measures. Investment proceeds are financing cash, not customer revenue, gross profit, or validation. When the active objective is immediate operating profit, the default allocation to investor outreach is JPY 0. Fundraising may be opened only by an explicit objective change and must not improve the revenue scorecard.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Capital follows verified customer behavior instead of development momentum.\n- The first JPY 300,000 can invalidate the segment, message, channel, or offer before the remaining JPY 2,700,000 is exposed.\n- cloud-itonami becomes the delivery and measurement substrate for a result-oriented service; its product breadth is not itself the sale.\n- Advertising is a scale mechanism after manual proof, not a substitute for discovery and closing.\n- The loop records both cash and founder effort, preventing apparently profitable work from hiding expensive delivery.\n- This ADR does not authorize live solicitation while a product commercial hard gate is red, nor does it authorize any specific external message or spend without the normal approval boundary.\n\n## Verification\n\nThe revenue-loop README and run template contain the tranche and unit-economics contract. Run 0020 records adoption. The scorecard identifies T1 as the active capital state and keeps the existing commercial gate explicit."}]
